loped at UC Berkeley as a successor to Ingres, it first appeared under the PostgreSQL name in 1996.\n\nPostgreSQL provides several indexing methods including B-tree, hash, GiST, and GIN. It supports both SQL and JSON query interfaces and uses multiversion concurrency control (MVCC) to handle concurrent access without read locks.\n\nPostgreSQL has built-in replication for high availability, supporting both logical and streaming modes. It can be extended with custom functions written in PL/pgSQL, Python, Perl, and other languages.\n\nSeveral derived products build on PostgreSQL. It is widely used in financial services and government, and competes with MySQL and Oracle Database.","originalFile":"PostgreSQL is an open-source relational database management system. The database engine supports ACID transactions, complex queries, and extensible data types. The RDBMS was originally developed at the University of California, Berkeley, as a successor to the Ingres project. The database system first appeared in 1996 under its current name.\n\nThe software platform provides several indexing methods including B-tree, hash, GiST, and GIN. The data management solution supports both SQL and JSON query interfaces. The storage engine uses multiversion concurrency control (MVCC) to handle concurrent access without read locks.\n\nThe relational engine offers built-in replication capabilities for high availability. The open-source platform supports logical and streaming replication modes. The database technology can be extended with custom functions written in PL/pgSQL, Python, Perl, and other languages.\n\nPostgreSQL serves as the foundation for several derived products. The enterprise solution has garnered significant adoption in financial services and government sectors. The data platform competes with other relational databases including MySQL and Oracle Database.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1,"newLines":7,"lines":["-PostgreSQL is an open-source relational database management system. The database engine supports ACID transactions, complex queries, and extensible data types. The RDBMS was originally developed at the University of California, Berkeley, as a successor to the Ingres project. The database system first appeared in 1996 under its current name.","+PostgreSQL is an open-source relational database. It supports ACID transactions, complex queries, and extensible data types. Originally developed at UC Berkeley as a successor to Ingres, it first appeared under the PostgreSQL name in 1996."," ","-The software platform provides several indexing methods including B-tree, hash, GiST, and GIN. The data management solution supports both SQL and JSON query interfaces. The storage engine uses multiversion concurrency control (MVCC) to handle concurrent access without read locks.","+PostgreSQL provides several indexing methods including B-tree, hash, GiST, and GIN. It supports both SQL and JSON query interfaces and uses multiversion concurrency control (MVCC) to handle concurrent access without read locks."," ","-The relational engine offers built-in replication capabilities for high availability. The open-source platform supports logical and streaming replication modes. The database technology can be extended with custom functions written in PL/pgSQL, Python, Perl, and other languages.","+PostgreSQL has built-in replication for high availability, supporting both logical and streaming modes. It can be extended with custom functions written in PL/pgSQL, Python, Perl, and other languages."," ","-PostgreSQL serves as the foundation for several derived products. The enterprise solution has garnered significant adoption in financial services and government sectors. The data platform competes with other relational databases including MySQL and Oracle Database.","+Several derived products build on PostgreSQL. It is widely used in financial services and government, and competes with MySQL and Oracle Database."]}],"userModifie